# Environment configuration example.
#
# No real secrets belong in this file or in this repository.
# Copy to .env locally and fill in real values; .env is gitignored.
#
# Frontend, database, queue and storage infrastructure have not been
# implemented yet. Actual configuration variables will be introduced by
# the tasks that implement each piece of infrastructure (TASK-003
# frontend, TASK-004 local environment, TASK-005 PostgreSQL, TASK-006
# Redis/queue).

# --- Application (backend, as of TASK-002) ---
# The authoritative Laravel environment template is backend/.env.example.
# Copy it to backend/.env and run `php artisan key:generate` inside
# backend/ — see backend/README.md.

# --- Database (target set in TASK-002; actual connectivity in TASK-005) ---
# backend/.env.example already targets DB_CONNECTION=pgsql (ADR-001) with
# local placeholder credentials; no PostgreSQL server is provisioned yet.

# --- Cache / Queue (to be defined in TASK-006) ---
# REDIS_HOST=

# --- File storage (to be defined when object storage adapter is implemented) ---
# FILESYSTEM_DISK=
